f sink operation ordering is unread.","A successful buffered write alone does not establish finalization or publication."],"source_ids":["file_snapshot.go:1:551"]},{"id":"snapshot_file_close","primary_activity":"A6","execution_owner":"Caller executing FileSnapshotSink.Close","protocol_context":"Finalization and publication of one file snapshot sink","trigger":"Close()","legal_preconditions":[],"implementation_guards":["Returns nil immediately if closed is already true.","Sets closed before attempting finalization."],"important_branches":["A finalize error triggers temporary-directory removal; a removal error replaces the finalize error returned to the caller.","Metadata or rename errors return without that cleanup branch.","Parent-directory or retention errors can occur after rename has published the directory.","A repeated Close returns nil even when the earlier Close failed."],"async_boundaries":[],"produces_fact_ids":["snapshot_file_rename_completed"],"consumes_fact_ids":[],"existing_protections":["The normal publication sequence flushes state and writes final size/CRC metadata before rename.","Synchronization is enabled by default; noSync is described as a private testing field."],"unknowns":["Crash durability depends on filesystem and operating-system behavior not established by these sources.","Caller interpretation of errors after publication and repeated Close success is unread.","Retention can subsequently remove a published snapshot; rename is not a guarantee of continued availability."],"source_ids":["file_snapshot.go:1:551"]},{"id":"snapshot_file_cancel","primary_activity":"A6","execution_owner":"Caller executing FileSnapshotSink.Cancel","protocol_context":"Cancellation of one file snapshot sink","trigger":"Cancel()","legal_preconditions":[],"implementation_guards":["Returns nil immediately when closed is already true.","Sets closed before finalization."],"important_branches":["A finalize error prevents the removal attempt.","Cancel after any Close attem